    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρεαττώ</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρεᾱτώ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦς</span>, ἡ, a court in Peiraeus, where banished men
		accused of murder were allowed to present themselves for trial, the
		accused being on board ship, the judges on shore; only dat. (loc.),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν Φρεαττοῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					23.77
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				78
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1300b29
			</span></i>:—the nom. is written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρεαττύς</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				1.28.11
			</span></i>.</div>
